# Cloudflare Pages reads this at the site root. Plain text, no build step.
#
# Pages' default for static assets is `max-age=14400` — four hours in which a
# returning visitor's browser serves CSS/JS from disk WITHOUT asking whether it
# changed. HTML is already `max-age=0`, so a deploy lands new markup against
# stale styles, and the PAIRING is what breaks: the 2026-08-08 theme rename
# shipped `data-theme="lilac"` to browsers still holding a themes.css that only
# knew `fairy`, and those rendered unstyled until the window expired. Mobile,
# with nothing cached, was fine — which is the tell for this whole class of bug.
#
# `must-revalidate` does NOT prevent it. That directive governs what a cache may
# do once a response is already stale; inside the freshness window the browser
# never asks at all.
#
# Purging the Cloudflare cache does not prevent it either. The stale copy is on
# the visitor's disk, not at the edge.
#
# ⚠ THIS FILE DID NOTHING UNTIL 2026-09-15. It was written with the rules
# `/*.css` and `/*.js`, and Pages silently ignored both: a `_headers` pattern
# takes a TRAILING splat (`/styles/*`), and `*` is not a glob you can put in the
# middle of a path or in front of an extension. Nothing warns you — the rule
# just never matches, and every asset keeps the 4h default. Caught by checking
# the live `Cache-Control` after a deploy, which is the only way to see it:
#
#   curl -sI https://deets.solutions/styles/main.css | grep -i cache-control
#
# Do that after touching this file. `max-age=0` is the rule working;
# `max-age=14400` is the rule being ignored again.
#
# So: revalidate every stylesheet and script, wherever it lives — one rule per
# directory that holds one. That is more lines than an extension glob, and it
# has the failure mode to match: a NEW tab with its own CSS or JS needs a line
# here, or it silently goes back to four hours. The per-tab and per-game assets
# (radio/radio.js, tanks/tanks.css, games/table.js) are exactly the ones that
# go stale the same way, so they are each listed. Each match costs one
# conditional request per load, answered with a ~100-byte 304 when nothing moved.
#
# The rules below are broader than CSS/JS — `/styles/*` catches everything in
# that directory. That is deliberate: these directories hold code, not media.
# The sprite and font directories are NOT listed, so they keep the 4h default.
#
# NOT covered, deliberately: the generated data files (sotd/songs.json,
# movies/movies.json). `/sotd/*` would now catch songs.json, so the JSONs are
# pinned back to the default underneath. A nightly refresh can be up to four
# hours late for a returning visitor — harmless for a once-a-day feed; drop
# those two rules if that ever reads as a bug.
#
# The alternative to all of this — versioned URLs (`chrome.css?v=…`) plus a long
# immutable max-age — is strictly faster and strictly easier to forget, since
# with no build step the stamping is manual. Revisit if the asset count ever
# makes the 304s worth avoiding.

/styles/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/js/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
  X-Deets-Probe: js-rule-matched

/games/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/deetsmusic/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/cities/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/mahjong/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/poker/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/tanks/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/radio/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/league/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/profile/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/sotd/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/movies/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

# The generated feeds, back to the 4h default (see the note above). A later
# rule wins in Pages' `_headers`, so these must stay below their directories.
/sotd/songs.json
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=14400

/movies/movies.json
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=14400
